.TH BEACOND 8 "August 2026" "beacond 1.4.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
beacond \- small heartbeat daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beacond
[\fB\-config\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beacond
is a small, dependency-free heartbeat daemon.
It reads a tiny config file, listens on a TCP address, and answers
.B /health
with a JSON status document and the running build version.
.PP
Under this package it runs as the unprivileged
.B beacon
system user via the
.B beacond.service
systemd unit, which is enabled and started automatically on install \(en see
.IR /usr/share/doc/beacond/README.Debian .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Path to the config file.
Default:
.IR /etc/beacond/beacond.yaml .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/beacond/beacond.yaml
Site configuration:
.B listen
(address to bind) and
.B log_level
(one of
.IR debug " or " info ).
Preserved across upgrades.
.TP
.I /var/log/beacond
Reserved for rotated log archives.
The daemon itself logs to stderr, which under systemd goes to the journal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR beacon-status (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
